// Calling a function value that arrived as an UN-ANNOTATED parameter and reached the calling
// frame as a CAPTURE, at a rep the all-i32 arity fallback cannot stand in for. `vl check`
// returns 0, and before D1634's capture channel the emitter refused with `emitProgram:
// function-value call arity has no interned signature` — the sig key resolved to "" outside
// the owning frame, so no `$fnsig` named the `(f64) => f64` functype the `call_ref` casts to.
//
// The f64 rep is why this is a probe and not a matrix cell: the i32 spelling of this program
// ran even while the key was unresolved, because the arity fallback happens to name the right
// functype there. Annotating the parameter also rescues it. See D1626.
// Should print 55.5.
function take(a) {
  const g = (m: f64) => a(m)
  print(g(54.0))
}
take((n: f64) => n + 1.5)
